W: 1. Braw, braw lads o' Galla Water,
W: Bonnie lads o' Galla Water;
W: I'll kilt my coats abune my knee,
W: And follow my love through the water;
W: Braw, braw lads.
W:
W: 2. Lothian lads are black as deils,
W: And Selkirk lads are no' much better;
W: I'll kilt my coats abune my knee
W: And follow the lad o' Galla Water;
W: Braw, braw lad.
W:
W: 3. It's ower the moss and doon yon glen,
W: And ower the bonnie blooming heather,
W: Nicht or day he bears the gree,
W: The bonnie lad o' Galla Water;
W: Braw, braw lad.
W:
W: 4. Corn rigs are fine and bonnie,
W: A block o' sheep is muckle better,
W: The wind will shake a field of oats
W: While lambs are frisklin' in Galla Water;
W: Braw, braw lads.
W:
W: 5. Adieu, soor plooms o' Galashiels,
W: Tae you, my faither, here's a letter;
W: It's I'm awa' wi' the black herd lad,
W: To bide wi' him in Galla Water;
W: Braw, braw lad.
%
